#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192464 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192746 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "e38c34ab-8ac6-5dd1-9812-e1a446e77ebf" :knowledge-point/title "Solving Two-Step Inequalities"}] :question/id #uuid "fef2e81e-33db-518d-91ad-a3d39637d736" :question/math-academy-id "e-10747" :question/problem "Represent the solution of the inequality $14 \\lt 5x-6$ on a number line." :question/worked-solution "First, we apply the addition principle, adding $6$ to both sides:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}14 & <5x-6 \\\\ 14+6 & <5x-6+6 \\\\ 20 & <5x+0 \\\\ 20 & <5x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSecond, we apply the multiplication principle, dividing both sides by $5{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}20 & <5x \\\\ \\frac{20}{5} & <\\frac{5x}{5} \\\\ \\frac{20}{5} & <\\frac{\\cancel{5}x}{\\cancel{5}} \\\\ 4 & <x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nFinally, let's swap the left and right-hand sides so that the variable is on the left-hand side. Remember that we also need to flip the inequality.\n\n$$\nx \\gt 4\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x  \\gt 4.$ The solution can be expressed on a number line, as shown below.\n\n![](images/3b/3b6c834b9f69e2610a3c61bb765ec0cba5ad03cfcd22a3ddb0290ff0fa3882f0.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192467 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192748 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "78151f63-63dc-5338-bf9b-90f3fd825173" :knowledge-point/title "Solving One-Step Inequalities When Flipping Is Required"}] :question/id #uuid "56743b65-6e81-557e-a0b6-e04dbe9fc7e4" :question/math-academy-id "e-10806" :question/problem "Represent the solution of the inequality $-6a > -12$ on a number line." :question/worked-solution "The variable $a$ is being *multiplied* by $-6.$ To isolate $a,$ we can perform the *opposite* operation, which is *dividing* by $-6.$ So, we divide both sides of the equation by $-6.$\n\nRemember, when multiplying or dividing by a negative number, we need to flip the inequality:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-6a\\,\\, & >\\,\\,-12 \\\\ \\frac{-6a}{-6}\\, & <\\,\\,\\frac{-12}{-6} \\\\ \\frac{-6a}{-6}\\, & <\\,\\,2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can cancel a common factor of $-6$ from both the numerator and denominator.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{-6a}{-6} & <2 \\\\ \\frac{\\cancel{-6}a}{\\cancel{-6}} & <2 \\\\ a & <2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $a<   2.$ The solution can be expressed on a number line, as shown below.\n\n![](images/2b/2b5947166eb517c08355c09c265f6a2c1f87bdafd776b2e03f5503585568b90b.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192492 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192768 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "9415209a-a06f-5d07-900f-7deb280837b5" :knowledge-point/title "Solving One-Step Inequalities"}] :question/id #uuid "5280bed5-8ca3-55e5-9a6b-af86bf858e0e" :question/math-academy-id "e-10945" :question/problem "Represent the solution of the inequality $k -12 \\lt  -5$ on a number line." :question/worked-solution "To isolate $k,$ we need to perform the *opposite* of *subtracting* $12,$ which is *adding* $12.$\nRemember to perform the same operation on the right-hand side.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}k-12 & <-5 \\\\ k-12+12 & <-5+12 \\\\ k+0 & <7 \\\\ k & <7\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $k \\lt  7.$ The solution can be expressed on a number line, as shown below.\n\n![](images/9c/9cc25f8eec7586ce65a17be3eb7af6ee509d014bf8dc9896cd45c6ef99769250.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186193124 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192768 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "9415209a-a06f-5d07-900f-7deb280837b5" :knowledge-point/title "Solving One-Step Inequalities"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "91dc0cc7-bdc2-55b3-bc63-cb9b07e57890" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/ba/bae522d2b6f5d1ddf58bfad76ca18d1e6057089bdc9063e7df4bad19a6339992.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186190631} {:answer/id #uuid "d125d33e-4ad5-5261-80ed-9eca6ff4e950" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/55/5598bc77f8244752fa80c8f70b4a03bc5de95415f9a35342d13264dd25f113d5.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186190632} {:answer/id #uuid "dcdbef40-b56b-5f58-a0ab-6d66d978379a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/70/709573d7c75c2cff50e771166fa4750609fb48d984b8095a363e866ae3cb584a.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186190633} {:answer/id #uuid "0c8ecb59-86e4-5e53-9709-8904d09403ab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/25/250658732778b386516d3b462f8d2f7010e871c2389a8e7c6e6de393627ec8a3.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186190634} {:answer/id #uuid "16b9b132-8e98-5a1d-8efc-d006ce72bc14" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/7d/7d898136f9b5ad8adfb0b2354c3b7b9630c7270440fafb481fbc860ee4fcc627.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186190635}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "16b9b132-8e98-5a1d-8efc-d006ce72bc14" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/7d/7d898136f9b5ad8adfb0b2354c3b7b9630c7270440fafb481fbc860ee4fcc627.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186190635} :answer-field/id #uuid "30efa466-e204-54a2-b0c5-4c39084a4945" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186190630}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "50d16bdb-fce1-5a97-8114-856a36da2d75" :question/math-academy-id "q-153603" :question/problem "Represent the solution of the inequality $a+5\\ge 11$ on a number line." :question/worked-solution "To isolate $a,$ we need to perform the *opposite* of *adding* $5,$ which is *subtracting* $5.$\nRemember to perform the same operation on the right-hand side.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a+5 & \\ge 11 \\\\ a+5-5 & \\ge 11-5 \\\\ a+0 & \\ge 6 \\\\ a & \\ge 6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $a\\ge 6.$ The solution can be expressed on a number line, as shown below.\n\n![](images/7d/7d898136f9b5ad8adfb0b2354c3b7b9630c7270440fafb481fbc860ee4fcc627.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186506542 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192748 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "78151f63-63dc-5338-bf9b-90f3fd825173" :knowledge-point/title "Solving One-Step Inequalities When Flipping Is Required"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "12d9ae4e-8ee9-5dab-a678-998b84633eec" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/14/1443d401eb2bd5a6a699f6c80fdd33f95270bed6e24d55165aff7b90bbd546b2.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186505947} {:answer/id #uuid "2d9ef012-bf37-5052-b96d-18f78871459b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/eb/ebda9e955c2613aa9e65b950ac80ad7ec4e52d6db6fdcce76cc2f89bbc20b0d4.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186505993} {:answer/id #uuid "364c3910-7df3-5411-bad0-d653131067da" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/7d/7d2e6671729b92d2ac42a357268a6545f1d3491c7c1a6133e7e460227c8a04da.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186506003} {:answer/id #uuid "93ee5e59-9e5d-5c6a-8a09-ad948704dae4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/35/3589e407d3ff892f4bfb00e73cf0c5e77a7fb4aaee39ecc3daeca53b60b49773.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186506162} {:answer/id #uuid "99281185-8a83-594a-94a5-070bba47ed34" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/94/944ad59d879c9eb7fbf08615659d5ac6a4b88ca37cb2dda50ccad7aa3f28046b.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186506178}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2d9ef012-bf37-5052-b96d-18f78871459b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/eb/ebda9e955c2613aa9e65b950ac80ad7ec4e52d6db6fdcce76cc2f89bbc20b0d4.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186505993} :answer-field/id #uuid "f308d5d5-0b30-5d3f-8d6d-a8777cb225e6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186506498}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "5f4cf73b-e442-544c-845a-c7e6521bdf69" :question/math-academy-id "q-155556" :question/problem "Represent the solution of the inequality $-\\frac{a}{4}>-2$ on a number line." :question/worked-solution "The variable $a$ is being *divided* by $4.$ To isolate $a$ and remove the negative sign, we *multiply* by $-4.$ \n\nRemember, when multiplying or dividing an inequality by a negative number, we need to flip the inequality sign:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{a}{4}\\,\\, & >\\,\\,-2 \\\\ (-4)\\cdot (-\\frac{a}{4})\\,\\, & <\\,\\,(-4)\\cdot (-2) \\\\ (-4)\\cdot (-\\frac{a}{4})\\,\\, & <\\,\\,8\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince two negative numbers multiply to give a positive number, we first cancel the negatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(-4)\\cdot (-\\frac{a}{4}) & <8 \\\\ (\\cancel{-}4)\\cdot (\\cancel{-}\\frac{a}{4}) & <8 \\\\ 4\\cdot \\frac{a}{4} & <8\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can cancel a common factor of $4$ from both the numerator and denominator.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4\\cdot \\frac{a}{4} & <8 \\\\ \\frac{4a}{4} & <8 \\\\ \\frac{\\cancel{4}a}{\\cancel{4}} & <8 \\\\ a & <8\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $a<8.$ The solution can be expressed on a number line, as shown below.\n\n \n\n![](images/eb/ebda9e955c2613aa9e65b950ac80ad7ec4e52d6db6fdcce76cc2f89bbc20b0d4.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186506545 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192746 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "e38c34ab-8ac6-5dd1-9812-e1a446e77ebf" :knowledge-point/title "Solving Two-Step Inequalities"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "01cf7ea8-3de1-5cae-9d52-a652bb86a99e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/7b/7bb94468ebcde9f65ca3192c5fe251c9a77c4548cce3bce62992a322d0469e65.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186505915} {:answer/id #uuid "37a5029c-6f03-58af-86ee-1d60ff82f949" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/5a/5a2b62f5f96850dbccb3c0d284d0b005069c82bba98c171b8bedb7c9377de5f2.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186506005} {:answer/id #uuid "56b8f5ba-6708-5ca9-b0cd-47a546aa1b20" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/19/19cce2d3039b99366d732bc3bdb9f0cae327413320049ddb1d9e1d9f763fe215.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186506059} {:answer/id #uuid "6713cb26-c5e6-589e-9365-8e54c4046e13" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/de/dec03ecdf937a3e9fb9c38671dcb704de97162d8306392dfbab9b956ad8b49af.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186506085} {:answer/id #uuid "72d5a6d0-1fb2-5bd9-9430-d6a20ae02ead" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/23/236731caee3bdbb7fee8922577a4945e97d81ee2876ca5b050c12654b2277a2a.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186506117}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "72d5a6d0-1fb2-5bd9-9430-d6a20ae02ead" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/23/236731caee3bdbb7fee8922577a4945e97d81ee2876ca5b050c12654b2277a2a.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186506117} :answer-field/id #uuid "6f08a84c-613a-541b-a1fa-a3771715b702" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186506428}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "6280d0e4-77c7-572f-9c1a-10c2908c012a" :question/math-academy-id "q-155561" :question/problem "Represent the solution of the inequality $-5x-7<-2$ on a number line." :question/worked-solution "First, we apply the addition principle, adding $7$ to both sides:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-5x-7 & <-2 \\\\ -5x-7+7 & <-2+7 \\\\ -5x+0 & <5 \\\\ -5x & <5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we apply the multiplication principle, dividing by $-5.$ \n\nRemember, when multiplying or dividing by a negative number, we need to flip the inequality:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-5x\\,\\, & <\\,\\,5 \\\\ \\frac{-5x}{-5}\\, & >\\,\\,\\frac{5}{-5} \\\\ \\frac{\\cancel{-5}x}{\\cancel{-5}}\\, & >\\,\\,-1 \\\\ x\\,\\, & >\\,\\,-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x>-1.$ The solution can be expressed on a number line, as shown below.\n\n![](images/23/236731caee3bdbb7fee8922577a4945e97d81ee2876ca5b050c12654b2277a2a.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186506583 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192746 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "e38c34ab-8ac6-5dd1-9812-e1a446e77ebf" :knowledge-point/title "Solving Two-Step Inequalities"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9db9c939-0e10-532b-9f82-1b953ae7623f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/c3/c3b46d339b4a8faffe148f083270236ac63ed5cd627fdedf83ae321cb08749ab.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186506186} {:answer/id #uuid "a0362577-a809-5212-97fc-f68b9c903158" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/44/447a65ae65d28c29d97170c576a4b5daf61345dfd5be6eafb677a59d9702f76a.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186506199} {:answer/id #uuid "a175f293-1509-584d-bc0c-d4cb84c90591" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/81/817328612514da56e2373483b7b579c5f8be03fb8b8ce182ec8220182a6bc9e7.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186506203} {:answer/id #uuid "ce9e0618-ec14-563b-be45-2904cff0fc80" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/7e/7e2c8543b9092501ef1a36289010f74e967b7a7238cfe9fe6904710cc0ffda08.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186506278} {:answer/id #uuid "f5afa12c-ba4a-51da-86ab-55010b4dfd33" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/34/34610901823137e2c15d3bf4515a7c700469f97cd876961b6ea8d9afadd1d14f.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186506362}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a175f293-1509-584d-bc0c-d4cb84c90591" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/81/817328612514da56e2373483b7b579c5f8be03fb8b8ce182ec8220182a6bc9e7.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186506203} :answer-field/id #uuid "ef7eddd3-cc10-50df-acb8-45b0b3fa44a0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186506497}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "bd2c58ff-4c4c-5b74-8ac8-2ec07ff5ad46" :question/math-academy-id "q-155565" :question/problem "Represent the solution of the inequality $4\\ge -3x+1$ on a number line." :question/worked-solution "First, we apply the addition principle, subtracting $1$ from both sides:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4 & \\ge -3x+1 \\\\ 4-1 & \\ge -3x+1-1 \\\\ 3 & \\ge -3x+0 \\\\ 3 & \\ge -3x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we apply the multiplication principle, dividing by $-3.$ \n\nRemember, when multiplying or dividing by a negative number, we need to flip the inequality:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3\\,\\, & \\ge \\,\\,-3x \\\\ \\frac{3}{-3}\\, & \\le \\,\\,\\frac{-3x}{-3} \\\\ -1\\, & \\le \\,\\,\\frac{\\cancel{-3}x}{\\cancel{-3}} \\\\ -1\\,\\, & \\le \\,\\,x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, let's swap the left and right-hand sides so that the variable is on the left-hand side. Remember, we also need to flip the inequality.\n\n$$\nx\\ge -1\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x\\ge -1.$ The solution can be expressed on a number line, as shown below.\n\n$$\n\n$$\n\n![](images/81/817328612514da56e2373483b7b579c5f8be03fb8b8ce182ec8220182a6bc9e7.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186506558 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192768 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "9415209a-a06f-5d07-900f-7deb280837b5" :knowledge-point/title "Solving One-Step Inequalities"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "04877aae-808d-5869-acc3-5a7836b0a7ca" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/7d/7dbfffa34020e124d15a87b94961bd3a9f4f437dc0596e8cc87c81e0544582dd.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186505923} {:answer/id #uuid "119d4a72-6df5-5dc3-8f43-96b52cce5fba" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/a7/a7df051043153eb7b88cfc4eb8af769f5d42dabf7c9e3dadd57986da8383374e.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186505944} {:answer/id #uuid "4594ab22-dba1-5ce6-bca6-9c4e4785457f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/8f/8f5c34779e0a05a0b1094261f7c7d221b14c2f2be16f08dab6903a465110e794.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186506028} {:answer/id #uuid "dc4c8a45-81fa-5e11-b89e-4e8e1f0a9b25" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/5a/5af366af2cb86131a092ae1ceae0087f6d5221faa6c376da9743c94ed09ba345.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186506306} {:answer/id #uuid "e00ed368-9d78-5b72-9f53-1e8cd4629c82" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/bd/bd4ccae5ea797d6c41e83c426b76491316552883e831bb82d82345d91773e4a3.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186506313}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e00ed368-9d78-5b72-9f53-1e8cd4629c82" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/bd/bd4ccae5ea797d6c41e83c426b76491316552883e831bb82d82345d91773e4a3.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186506313} :answer-field/id #uuid "ccb8edc4-f1cb-5fa3-8c77-760f79763cca" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186506481}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "82b4f2d5-49e5-54a4-9867-0518a805773f" :question/math-academy-id "q-156657" :question/problem "Represent the solution of the inequality $5z\\le -45$ on a number line." :question/worked-solution "The variable $z$ is being *multiplied* by $5.$ To isolate $z$, we can perform the *opposite* operation, which is *dividing* by $5.$ So, we divide both sides of the equation by $5.$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5z & \\le -45 \\\\ \\frac{5z}{5} & \\le \\frac{-45}{5} \\\\ \\frac{5z}{5} & \\le -9\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can cancel a common factor of $5$ from the numerator and denominator.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{5z}{5} & \\le -9 \\\\ \\frac{\\cancel{5}z}{\\cancel{5}} & \\le -9 \\\\ z & \\le -9\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $z\\le -9.$ The solution can be expressed on a number line, as shown below.\n\n![](images/bd/bd4ccae5ea797d6c41e83c426b76491316552883e831bb82d82345d91773e4a3.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186506551 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192748 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "78151f63-63dc-5338-bf9b-90f3fd825173" :knowledge-point/title "Solving One-Step Inequalities When Flipping Is Required"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5d969f3e-15f3-5209-9cde-8047f9535b21" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/77/77cd7409394f178fa727b38008d26d3961e2e753303a058ca6aa29b4ea113424.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186506074} {:answer/id #uuid "5daf1180-56a8-52e9-8381-542f6885592e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/3f/3fae3905deb78b9f5f1ea01717b7d4bc9cc21e560afb98d070bd0c6cb43c6dee.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186506075} {:answer/id #uuid "6f23c623-b0ea-569e-9455-1c5116ebfbb6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/ed/ed2bdc2c6fb877dd611c160ef902b8eeeaaabb49485e2e62695fcfd3a8bc2652.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186506111} {:answer/id #uuid "e16b964a-0b5e-5b64-945a-fb48cdd1a7f7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/ba/ba9e71603b1f780d8213d89f19242fba69a46c186f99e3657d874c3ce8e62bf4.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186506321} {:answer/id #uuid "e7128377-c9ba-5a5b-9cde-64304bb2282b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/a6/a622d3f7ef117b60b5dd3744cd7c322235ead95ffd3ca806adc1e37a22014c0f.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186506333}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e7128377-c9ba-5a5b-9cde-64304bb2282b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/a6/a622d3f7ef117b60b5dd3744cd7c322235ead95ffd3ca806adc1e37a22014c0f.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186506333} :answer-field/id #uuid "1dc56f59-f723-54a0-80fa-3788b2766711" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186506390}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "70d3487e-b503-50e8-b857-c63dd534d65a" :question/math-academy-id "q-156665" :question/problem "Represent the solution of the inequality $-5t>15$ on a number line." :question/worked-solution "The variable $t$ is being *multiplied* by $-5.$ To isolate $t,$ we can perform the *opposite* operation, which is *dividing* by $-5.$ So, we divide both sides of the equation by $-5.$\n\nRemember, when multiplying or dividing by a negative number, we need to flip the inequality:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-5t\\,\\, & >\\,\\,15 \\\\ \\frac{-5t}{-5}\\, & <\\,\\,\\frac{15}{-5} \\\\ \\frac{-5t}{-5}\\, & <\\,\\,-3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can cancel a common factor of $-5$ from both the numerator and denominator.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{-5t}{-5} & <-3 \\\\ \\frac{\\cancel{-5}t}{\\cancel{-5}} & <-3 \\\\ t & <-3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $t<-3.$ The solution can be expressed on a number line, as shown below.\n\n![](images/a6/a622d3f7ef117b60b5dd3744cd7c322235ead95ffd3ca806adc1e37a22014c0f.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186193331 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192746 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "e38c34ab-8ac6-5dd1-9812-e1a446e77ebf" :knowledge-point/title "Solving Two-Step Inequalities"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8ea069f9-3cc1-5eda-bf89-7438f8d2a4d6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/b7/b781c7a965fb2af706fcb37c0a9a2648c204e461bcbfb958ef08891dd295b1d3.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186191914} {:answer/id #uuid "b89d2970-14ca-5a0f-b3b5-9071c0129e24" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/d8/d8bf2efe27b88ed710cd08a2ede3d91eb5c01886a5e48427801299909121adcd.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186191915} {:answer/id #uuid "d54c2416-07ee-533b-8dc3-2245d5525a38" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/5f/5f879e8107828488345adb0553163100de60ae727a022b0bebf0009061b3b686.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186191916} {:answer/id #uuid "f91f6c87-3664-5989-9586-026c7a161613" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/b0/b02bead6d12049fedcf78bea9558a7c95ee85d78f801e41c46ea653ba1712750.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186191917} {:answer/id #uuid "3f629ce9-741b-558c-ac42-88466159f545" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/e1/e1ed07e830ce01e84f020e8a17b8f545ad0285f71f6778ab7f0c390ae3ef5fa6.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186191918}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f91f6c87-3664-5989-9586-026c7a161613" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/b0/b02bead6d12049fedcf78bea9558a7c95ee85d78f801e41c46ea653ba1712750.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186191917} :answer-field/id #uuid "01a5d9ac-127b-50c2-9b44-71a34aca95d6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186191913}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "6c6d1514-6076-5c4c-b1eb-5ffebb170632" :question/math-academy-id "q-44742" :question/problem "Represent the solution of the inequality $4x+2\\le 10$ on a number line." :question/worked-solution "First, we apply the addition principle, subtracting $2$ from both sides:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4x+2 & \\le 10 \\\\ 4x+2-2 & \\le 10-2 \\\\ 4x+0 & \\le 8 \\\\ 4x & \\le 8\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSecond, we apply the multiplication principle, dividing both sides by $4:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4x & \\le 8 \\\\ \\frac{4x}{4} & \\le \\frac{8}{4} \\\\ \\frac{\\cancel{4}x}{\\cancel{4}} & \\le \\frac{8}{4} \\\\ x & \\le 2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, the solution is $x\\le 2.$ The solution can be expressed on a number line, as shown below.\n\n![](images/b0/b02bead6d12049fedcf78bea9558a7c95ee85d78f801e41c46ea653ba1712750.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186506570 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192746 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "e38c34ab-8ac6-5dd1-9812-e1a446e77ebf" :knowledge-point/title "Solving Two-Step Inequalities"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8733ee62-58f4-5707-b765-cd0aee979d81" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/b9/b92ce4122ef412dd99aedba0bd4d01449dc1bf4ad2a9e40bb8894ebdd8fa3593.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186506147} {:answer/id #uuid "ce471c74-dd80-5207-8b46-cc54ae26d8f3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/66/66c332853de6ddf9494186fec7ee384c84b577d16908daf488882b8d53cb122e.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186506277} {:answer/id #uuid "ceb5af45-a7ca-5c8b-b035-a42871ca6fa0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/49/4962a3a0904dd7d45a83f82e3708adeb9274b80c11849f563e630f8b198a72dc.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186506279} {:answer/id #uuid "e1c76ece-2740-52eb-911f-2c79fc0be91c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/ca/cae0dff0348d79e848762a89b920c8eee1b5489c9258cc6bf4bf50e74b21e710.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186506322} {:answer/id #uuid "f827a8b1-2175-5e30-bf37-0dfcab286741" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/b9/b92b3f18e34d94007facc917c8675d9e7fb62e4f3a33e0aa36afce5a2cc90a32.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186506365}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8733ee62-58f4-5707-b765-cd0aee979d81" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/b9/b92ce4122ef412dd99aedba0bd4d01449dc1bf4ad2a9e40bb8894ebdd8fa3593.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186506147} :answer-field/id #uuid "de782307-e385-5716-91a7-af2fcc5b4f7c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186506490}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "93f851d7-f3f4-511e-adef-c16fd42c2432" :question/math-academy-id "q-44781" :question/problem "Represent the solution of the inequality $-2x+3\\le 7$ on a number line." :question/worked-solution "First, we apply the addition principle, subtracting $3$ from both sides:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-2x+3 & \\le 7 \\\\ -2x+3-3 & \\le 7-3 \\\\ -2x+0 & \\le 4 \\\\ -2x & \\le 4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we apply the multiplication principle, dividing by $-2.$ \n\nRemember, when multiplying or dividing by a negative number, we need to flip the inequality:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-2x\\,\\, & \\le \\,\\,4 \\\\ \\frac{-2x}{-2}\\, & \\ge \\,\\,\\frac{4}{-2} \\\\ \\frac{\\cancel{-2}x}{\\cancel{-2}}\\, & \\ge \\,\\,-2 \\\\ x\\,\\, & \\ge \\,\\,-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x\\ge -2.$ The solution can be expressed on a number line, as shown below.\n\n![](images/b9/b92ce4122ef412dd99aedba0bd4d01449dc1bf4ad2a9e40bb8894ebdd8fa3593.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186193332 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192746 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "e38c34ab-8ac6-5dd1-9812-e1a446e77ebf" :knowledge-point/title "Solving Two-Step Inequalities"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "aefc84df-613e-5647-aa10-8ac88f939fdd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/62/6270d597864a8b03d823eff9362a5264654962b14e15853572d6de442d7ad20c.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186191920} {:answer/id #uuid "ba74e3c7-3c31-51fd-81ea-10c17a0b432a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/55/55eb9bd17fd57f8916166ed40e9acb1bfef9ccee42c482265acb2a7c882b6c8b.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186191921} {:answer/id #uuid "f5f7e108-8160-5313-af54-110164172d1e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/26/26a95d6bdbaa038986b7058e31d44ac77c1367f7f5b21086cd9eb2169cb40f4d.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186191922} {:answer/id #uuid "20757c65-2ea5-51ab-bcd0-468c9b824f1b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/34/34610901823137e2c15d3bf4515a7c700469f97cd876961b6ea8d9afadd1d14f.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186191923} {:answer/id #uuid "33aede55-ff5d-50e2-9aaf-69bb43fe8676" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/66/6689d28358a20b8ed5a7a2b4f865bc3967afaea1ae83405fd792b2fd9f261032.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186191924}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "20757c65-2ea5-51ab-bcd0-468c9b824f1b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/34/34610901823137e2c15d3bf4515a7c700469f97cd876961b6ea8d9afadd1d14f.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186191923} :answer-field/id #uuid "831cfcf5-d81c-5697-913a-286a6e501166" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186191919}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "a4887090-9abd-5cb8-9f83-e31b843cdaa8" :question/math-academy-id "q-44882" :question/problem "Represent the solution of the inequality $-3x+2\\ge 5$ on a number line." :question/worked-solution "First, we apply the addition principle, subtracting $2$ from both sides:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-3x+2 & \\ge 5 \\\\ -3x+2-2 & \\ge 5-2 \\\\ -3x+0 & \\ge 3 \\\\ -3x & \\ge 3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we apply the multiplication principle, dividing by $-3.$ \n\nRemember, when multiplying or dividing by a negative number, we need to flip the inequality:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-3x\\,\\, & \\ge \\,\\,3 \\\\ \\frac{-3x}{-3}\\, & \\le \\,\\,\\frac{3}{-3} \\\\ \\frac{\\cancel{-3}x}{\\cancel{-3}}\\, & \\le \\,\\,-1 \\\\ x\\,\\, & \\le \\,\\,-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x\\le -1.$ The solution can be expressed on a number line, as shown below.\n\n$$\n\n$$\n\n![](images/34/34610901823137e2c15d3bf4515a7c700469f97cd876961b6ea8d9afadd1d14f.png)"}]}
